{"name":"Dizzy Days","hex":"#d14e2f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"dizzy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Experiencing a sensation of whirling and of being giddy, unbalanced, or lightheaded.","Producing giddiness."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make (someone or something) dizzy; to bewilder."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dizzy"},{"term":"days","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of day"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A particular time or period of vague extent.","Life."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/days"}],"entries":[{"title":"Dizziness","blocks":[{"text":"Dizziness is an imprecise term that can refer to a sense of disorientation in space, vertigo, or lightheadedness. It can also refer to disequilibrium or a non-specific feeling, such as giddiness or foolishness."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/Depiction_of_a_person_feeling_dizzy.png/330px-Depiction_of_a_person_feeling_dizzy.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dizziness"},{"title":"Day","blocks":[{"text":"A day is the time period of a full rotation of the Earth with respect to the Sun. On average, this is 24 hours. As a day passes at a given location it experiences morning, afternoon, evening, and night. This daily cycle drives circadian rhythms in many organisms, which are vital to many life processes."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Day"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Midtown_Manhattan_from_Weehawken_September_2021_panorama_1.jpg/500px-Midtown_Manhattan_from_Weehawken_September_2021_panorama_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Midtown_Manhattan_from_Weehawken_September_2021_panorama_1.jpg/1280px-Midtown_Manhattan_from_Weehawken_September_